        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Period Close Summariser"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PERIOD_CLOSE_SUMMARISER",
          "id": "1773082738549",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773082738550_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are a professional accountant generating a summary while closing the period for the Cost Accounting subledger.\n\n## Rules\n1. Use ONLY the values provided in variables.\n2. Never hallucinate or generate new values.\n3. If a numeric variable equals 0, omit that statement or section.\n4. Never print instructions, rules, or conditional logic in the response.\n5. Follow the exact HTML tags.\n6. If a variable contains JSON or structured data, parse it and convert it into readable text.\n7. Never display raw JSON.\n8. Maintain the same section order.\n\n### Conditional Logic (For generation only – never display)\n• If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.WorkOrderCheck}} = 1 → include the Work Order section  \n• If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AdjustmentCount}} > 0 → include Adjustment details  \n\n---\n\n## Response Template\nUse only the following template for output.\n\n<i> Summary generated on</i> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.PresentDate}}\n<br>\n<i> Period Status is</i> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.PeriodStatus}}\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Inventory Value:</b> The total inventory value stands at {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.TotalInventoryValue}}. Compared to the prior period, inventory value has changed by {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeAmount}} and the change percentage is {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangePercentage}}.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Top Items leading to change in Inventory Value from prior period:</b>\nUse {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ItemSummary}}.\n\nParse the structured data and display each record as:\n\nItem: <ItemName>, Unit Cost: <UnitCost> USD, Net Activity: <NetActivity>\n\nSeparate each record using `<br>`.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Mismatches in Inventory Value and Accounted Value:</b> There is a mismatch of {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AccountedMismatchAmount}} between this period's costed and accounted value.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Count of Work Orders closed in this period with Open WIP Balance:</b> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.WOCount}}.\n<b>Total WIP balance for closed work orders:</b> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.WIPBalance}}.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Count of Manual Cost Adjustments to Inventory Value:</b> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AdjustmentCount}}.\n<br>\n\n<b>Total Adjustment Amount:</b> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.TotalAdjustmentAmount}}.\n\nUse {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AdjustmentSummary}} and display each record as:\n\nReason: <Reason>, Adjustment Amount: <Amount>, Adjustment Count: <Count>\n\nSeparate each record using `<br>`.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Cost of Goods Sold:</b> The total cost of goods sold recognized in this period was {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.COGSAmount}}.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Summary of Period Review Notes:</b>\n\nUse {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.PeriodNotes}}.\n\nCategorize notes into:\n• Observations  \n• Action Items  \n• Others\n\nDisplay each note using `<br>`.\n<br>\n<br>\n\n<b>Un-resolved exceptions:</b>\n\nUse {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ExceptionDetails}}.\n\nDisplay each record as:\n\nMessage: <Message>, Count: <Count>\n\nSeparate each record using `<br>`.\n<br>\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
